    {
      "id": "K_xmH7juKSKpu3jhq6l1H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 358,
      "y": 727,
      "width": 925.0550537109375,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1292714325,
      "version": 305,
      "versionNonce": 1126942261,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783432581231,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "If queries are fixed pre-known, expectation is always Real-Time/Near Real-time\nIf ad-hoc, delay acceptable.\n\n\nOLAP Cons:\nfreshness, Immutable , Realtime Inserts slow (to handle fast write , seperate kafka streams pipeline needed - costly) ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "If queries are fixed pre-known, expectation is always Real-Time/Near Real-time\nIf ad-hoc, delay acceptable.\n\n\nOLAP Cons:\nfreshness, Immutable , Realtime Inserts slow (to handle fast write , seperate kafka streams pipeline needed - costly) ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JsLWU5tJeiYI_0t4w3OOm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 349.57142857142844,
      "y": 898,
      "width": 2389.678466796875,
      "height": 1380,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1775264469,
      "version": 3162,
      "versionNonce": 1247640846,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783592534581,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\nEntity : (dim1 , dim2 , dim3)\n<single/multi-dimention filters> + <aggregation full/bucketted> + <sort/limit>\n\nURL-Shortner:\n    getTotalClicksForURL\n        (filter by urlID) + (aggregation full) \nCamelcamelcamel:\n    getPricesForProductWithinTimeWindow\n        (filter by productId & ts) + (aggregation bucketted {flooredTs}) + (sort by ts)\nTop-K:\n    getTopKVideoIds:\n        () + (aggregation bucketted {videoId}) + (sort & limit)\nAd-click aggregator:\n    getClicksForAdWithinTimeWindow\n        same as camel, here writes TPS very high\n\nEvery other major application like insta/uber etc has analytics - where OLAP is used\n    \nzero filters , \n    no aggregation: \n        no sorting: NA (Full table view)\n        with sorting:\n    full aggregation: \n        no sorting:\n        with sorting:\n    bucketted aggregation : \n        no sorting:\n        with sorting: topK   ( - , COUNT(videoId) , COUNT(videoId) )\nsingle filter \n    no aggregation: \n        no sorting: Every System\n        with sorting:\n    full : \n        no sorting: url-shortner (urlId , COUNT(*) , - )\n        with sorting:\n    bucketted : \n        no sorting: url-shortner ( urlId, COUNT(country), - )\n        with sorting: camel (productId, AVG(ts) , ts)\nmulti filter\n    no aggregation: \n        no sorting: Many Systems\n        sorting:\n    full aggregation : \n        no sorting: url-shortner ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(country) , - ) - bar graph\n        with sorting: url-shortner ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(country) , COUNT(country) ) - topk chart\n    bucketted aggregation : \n        no sorting:\n        sorting:\n\n\nWrite TPS is also one other dimension for above query based decision graph\n\nUsually when aggreagations present then filter willl be pk & ts , so having groupby has no impact on design ? - YES, grouping doesnt change the design at all\n    Also bucketing = grouping on ts, so even bucketing doesnt have an impact.\nSo queries are :\n    non-analytical queries : multi-dimention filters , but no dimentional explosion as combinations of dimentions are fixed - (filters,-,maybe)\n    analytical queries: (pk , agg with/without grouping , maybe)  or  ( {pk,ts} , agg with/without grouping , maybe)\n        Ex:\n            url-shortner :  (urlId , COUNT(*) , - ) ,   ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(*) GROUPTBY(country) , - ) , ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(*) GROUPTBY(country) , count)\n\n    one case to note:\n        total clicks in india:\n            2 approaches : \n                1. filter frist & then agg   or \n                2. agg & then filter\n            For analytical dshboards, we dont usually support this kind of queries, instead we shown clicksPerCountry graph. But if really needed can follow either 1 or 2. Both will have same TC unless indexed for 1. But usually we dont index for analytical queries, unless very few quereies we are supporting\n            For non-analytical, i.e very few queries in the system, then add an index and follow 1.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\nEntity : (dim1 , dim2 , dim3)\n<single/multi-dimention filters> + <aggregation full/bucketted> + <sort/limit>\n\nURL-Shortner:\n    getTotalClicksForURL\n        (filter by urlID) + (aggregation full) \nCamelcamelcamel:\n    getPricesForProductWithinTimeWindow\n        (filter by productId & ts) + (aggregation bucketted {flooredTs}) + (sort by ts)\nTop-K:\n    getTopKVideoIds:\n        () + (aggregation bucketted {videoId}) + (sort & limit)\nAd-click aggregator:\n    getClicksForAdWithinTimeWindow\n        same as camel, here writes TPS very high\n\nEvery other major application like insta/uber etc has analytics - where OLAP is used\n    \nzero filters , \n    no aggregation: \n        no sorting: NA (Full table view)\n        with sorting:\n    full aggregation: \n        no sorting:\n        with sorting:\n    bucketted aggregation : \n        no sorting:\n        with sorting: topK   ( - , COUNT(videoId) , COUNT(videoId) )\nsingle filter \n    no aggregation: \n        no sorting: Every System\n        with sorting:\n    full : \n        no sorting: url-shortner (urlId , COUNT(*) , - )\n        with sorting:\n    bucketted : \n        no sorting: url-shortner ( urlId, COUNT(country), - )\n        with sorting: camel (productId, AVG(ts) , ts)\nmulti filter\n    no aggregation: \n        no sorting: Many Systems\n        sorting:\n    full aggregation : \n        no sorting: url-shortner ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(country) , - ) - bar graph\n        with sorting: url-shortner ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(country) , COUNT(country) ) - topk chart\n    bucketted aggregation : \n        no sorting:\n        sorting:\n\n\nWrite TPS is also one other dimension for above query based decision graph\n\nUsually when aggreagations present then filter willl be pk & ts , so having groupby has no impact on design ? - YES, grouping doesnt change the design at all\n    Also bucketing = grouping on ts, so even bucketing doesnt have an impact.\nSo queries are :\n    non-analytical queries : multi-dimention filters , but no dimentional explosion as combinations of dimentions are fixed - (filters,-,maybe)\n    analytical queries: (pk , agg with/without grouping , maybe)  or  ( {pk,ts} , agg with/without grouping , maybe)\n        Ex:\n            url-shortner :  (urlId , COUNT(*) , - ) ,   ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(*) GROUPTBY(country) , - ) , ( (urlId,device) , COUNT(*) GROUPTBY(country) , count)\n\n    one case to note:\n        total clicks in india:\n            2 approaches : \n                1. filter frist & then agg   or \n                2. agg & then filter\n            For analytical dshboards, we dont usually support this kind of queries, instead we shown clicksPerCountry graph. But if really needed can follow either 1 or 2. Both will have same TC unless indexed for 1. But usually we dont index for analytical queries, unless very few quereies we are supporting\n            For non-analytical, i.e very few queries in the system, then add an index and follow 1.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
